{"created": "2025-03-30T13:38:36.640813+00:00", "modified": "2025-03-30T13:38:37.031869+00:00", "id": 15108715, "conceptrecid": "12588358", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15108715", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.12588358", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15108715", "metadata": {"title": "OPSSAT-AD - anomaly detection dataset for satellite telemetry", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15108715", "publication_date": "2024-06-24", "description": "<p>This is the AI-ready benchmark dataset (OPSSAT-AD) containing the telemetry data acquired on board OPS-SAT---a CubeSat mission that has been operated by the European Space Agency.</p>\n<p>It is accompanied by the paper with baseline results obtained using 30 supervised and unsupervised classic and deep machine learning algorithms for anomaly detection. They were trained and validated using the training-test dataset split introduced in this work, and we present a suggested set of quality metrics that should always be&nbsp;calculated to confront the new algorithms for anomaly detection while exploiting OPSSAT-AD. We believe that this work may become an important step toward building a fair, reproducible, and objective validation procedure that can be used to quantify the capabilities of the emerging anomaly detection techniques in an unbiased and fully transparent way.</p>\n<p>The included files are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>segments.csv</code> with the acquired telemetry signals from ESA OPS-SAT aircraft,</li>\n<li><code>dataset.csv</code> with the extracted, synthetic features are computed for each manually split and labeled telemetry segment.</li>\n<li>code files for data processing and example modeliing (<code>dataset_generator.ipynb</code> for data processing, <code>modeling_examples.ipynb</code> with simple examples, &nbsp;<code>requirements.txt</code>- with details on Python configuration, and the&nbsp;<code>LICENSE</code> file)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Please have a look at our two papers commenting on this dataset:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The benchmark paper with results of 30 supervised and unsupervised anomaly detection models for this collection:<br>Ruszczak, B., Kotowski. K., Nalepa, J., Evans, D.:<strong> The OPS-SAT benchmark for detecting anomalies in satellite telemetry, 2024</strong>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.04730\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">preprint arxiv: 2407.04730</a>,</li>\n<li>the conference paper in which we presented some preliminary results for this dataset:<br>Ruszczak, B., Kotowski. K., Andrzejewski, J., et al.: (2023). Machine Learning Detects Anomalies in OPS-SAT Telemetry. Computational Science &ndash; ICCS 2023. LNCS, vol 14073. Springer, Cham, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-35995-8_21\">DOI:10.1007/978-3-031-35995-8_21</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Bogdan, Ruszczak", "affiliation": "Opole University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0003-1089-1778"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Ruszczak, Bogdan", "affiliation": "Opole University of Technology", "type": "Researcher", "orcid": "0000-0003-1089-1778"}, {"name": "Kotowski, Krzysztof", "affiliation": "KP Labs", "type": "Researcher", "orcid": "0000-0003-2596-6517"}, {"name": "Evans, David", "affiliation": "European Space Agency", "type": "Researcher", "orcid": "0009-0006-1790-5238"}, {"name": "Nalepa, Jakub", "affiliation": "Silesian University of Technology", "type": "Researcher", "orcid": "0000-0002-4026-1569"}], "keywords": ["anomaly detection", "machine learning", "deep learning", "unsupervised learning", "supervised learning", "European Space Agency", "ESA", "telemetry", "signal processing"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "arXiv:2407.04730", "relation": "documents", "resource_type": "publication-journal", "scheme": "arxiv"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/978-3-031-35995-8_21", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-conferencepaper", "scheme": "doi"}], "references": ["Ruszczak, B., Kotowski. K., Evans, D., Nalepa, J.: The OPS-SAT benchmark for detecting anomalies in satellite telemetry, 2024, arXiv: https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.04730", "Ruszczak, B., Kotowski. K., Andrzejewski, J., et al.: (2023). Machine Learning Detects Anomalies in OPS-SAT Telemetry. Computational Science \u2013 ICCS 2023. LNCS, vol 14073. Springer, Cham, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-35995-8_21"], "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/kplabs-pl/OPS-SAT-AD", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "jupyter_notebook", "title": {"en": "Jupyter Notebook"}}, {"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "4000137339/22/NL/GLC/ov", "internal_id": "03wd9za21::4000137339/22/NL/GLC/ov", "funder": {"name": "European Space Agency"}, "title": "On-board Anomaly detection from the OPS-SAT telemetry using deep learning"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "12588358"}}]}}, "title": "OPSSAT-AD - anomaly detection dataset for satellite telemetry", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15108715", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15108715", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15108715?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15108715", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15108715", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15108715", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15108715/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/12588358", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/12588358", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.12588358", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.12588358", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15108715/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15108715/sequence/default", "files": "http